# opengl32: Implement wow64 opengl buffer-mapping on MESA_map_buffer_client_pointer
# https://gitlab.winehq.org/wine/wine/-/merge_requests/11579 state=closed
# See https://github.com/KhronosGroup/OpenGL-Registry/pull/680 and https://github.com/KhronosGroup/OpenGL-Registry/pull/678 .

The main benefit of this approach is the simplicity on the wine side and allowing drivers to maintain control of buffer mapping logic, which can be particularly complex in non-persistent paths. (see for example https://gitlab.winehq.org/wine/wine/-/merge_requests/11343#note_145372)

Fixes https://bugs.winehq.org/show_bug.cgi?id=58834

Wait to merge this until we get driver support. Zink support is well on its way https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/43297 , and the RadeonSI implementation, which is simpler, I'll submit afterwards.
